  "notes": "{跪|ひざまず}く is a formal verb indicating the act of kneeling, typically associated with showing respect, worship, or making formal requests.\n\nCONJUGATION (godan verb):\n- {跪|ひざまず}く (dictionary form)\n- {跪|ひざまず}かない (negative)\n- {跪|ひざまず}いた (past)\n- {跪|ひざまず}いて (te-form)\n\nUSAGE:\nThis word is more literary/formal than simply saying ⟦{膝|ひざ}→膝：00940_hiza⟧⟦を→を：00422_wo⟧⟦つく→付く：01960_tsuku⟧ (to put one's knees down). It emphasizes the reverent or submissive nature of the action.",
